invariant: INV-4
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_session
reason: hsf_begin draws the ClientHello random from ch_rand_bytes, with a
  declaration of its own because a RAND=session build's rand.h declares
  none, where every draw goes through rand_draw to the session's source.
  A RAND=session object would then import a hook no image defines, and
  the hello random would not be the client's own. The session loop counts
  one draw at the hook and one fewer at the client's source, and the
  random on the wire is not the source's second draw.

--- old
    rand_draw(&t->cfg, h->random, sizeof h->random);
#ifdef CH_KEX_HYBRID
--- new
    void ch_rand_bytes(uint8_t *p, size_t n);
    ch_rand_bytes(h->random, sizeof h->random);
#ifdef CH_KEX_HYBRID
